You are assuming that NPC's would be implemented in real-time as well.
I see no reason that you could not implement a multi-user NetHack following
the same ideas that most muds use... watch for activity on socket connections
and take action when you see some.  The only Bad Thing you'd have to worry
about would be what happens while you are paralyzed (and perhaps holding down
space to skim over your 200 ticks), and another player wanders in?  Of course
*I* don't see that as a problem <evil grin>.

